course: dictionary
lesson: 6212
title: One wrong step
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A misstep is a wrong step. When you are walking, a misstep can make you trip or fall. The word is made of two parts: mis-, which often means wrong, and step.
explain: The word can also mean a mistake in what you do or decide. Look at the example: «A misstep» means a mistake. Ask yourself, what word could go in its place? A mistake fits, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Context tells you how big the misstep is. «One misstep on the ice» means one slip can cause a fall. «A costly misstep» means a mistake that loses something valuable, such as time, money or a game.
fact: A misstep is a wrong step when walking, which can make you trip or fall.
fact: A misstep is also a mistake in what you do or decide.
fact: «A misstep» means a mistake.
fact: The prefix mis- often means wrong or badly, as in misspell and misread.
fact: Common phrases: «one misstep» means one small mistake; «a costly misstep» means a mistake that loses a lot.
exercise: What does misstep mean in «A misstep» means a mistake? | A kind of shoe | *A mistake | A dance move | A long walk
exercise: «One misstep on the wet stairs and Leo fell.» What does misstep mean here? | A loud shout | A fast run up the stairs | A shiny, wet floor | *A wrong step that makes you trip
exercise: «The leader's misstep cost the team the game.» What does misstep mean here? | *A bad decision that caused a mistake | A new leader chosen by the team | A happy team dance | A cheer for the winning side
test: Which phrase means one small mistake? | a long walk | a wet stair | a loud shout | *one misstep
test: Using the prefix mis- as a clue, which word means spelled wrongly? | mislead | misplace | *misspell | misread
exam: Read «a costly misstep». Which option best explains it? | A step taken very slowly | A quiet walk | A cheap shoe | *A mistake that loses a lot
